HST Office: Conditional Formatting uses Excel's rule types and Rules Manager order
(owner-approved Microsoft Office parity for beta.5).

- The rule type list holds: all cells by value, cells that contain, top or bottom ranked, above or below
  average, unique or duplicate, a formula, dates. The condition list shows the conditions of its rule type
  only; all 24 conditions are still reachable. A saved rule opens on the type that holds its condition.
- Manage Conditional Formatting lists the rule first, then the range it applies to.

Rules still apply cell styles rather than direct formats, and there is no Stop If True: both differ from
Excel by design of the engine and were not part of the approved scope.

License: these upstream files remain under their original license (MPL-2.0).
Test: tests/runtime/check-dialogs-sheets.py (conditional-format).
